  "body": "Main is red since `d94c65fcf`: the step `motion suites: finish3d_hop_height` fails. This PR fixes the cause in `camcraft-sim` and does not change a test assertion.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe fault is not an interaction of two merges. PR #4108 (#4062, merge `7b2587e15`) causes it alone. The post-merge run on `7b2587e15` (run 45871450597) already shows this failure. That run ended after the run on `d94c65fcf`, so the issue names `d94c65fcf` (#4198, which does not touch this code) as the first red commit. The run on the parent `26c626bb3` does not have this failure.\n\n#4108 adds a finished-part sweep of the vertical rapids for `Mode::Envelope` paths (`vertical_rapid_hits` in `crates/sim/src/verify/solid.rs`). This sweep judges the whole cutter at the start pose of each vertical rapid. A 3D finish pass ends with the ball on the model. The finish law permits a contact up to the finish tolerance there. The retract up from that pose then starts \"in the part\", and the verifier gives `RapidInPart`. The quick gate of #4108 did not run the motion suite, because the diff touched only `sim` and `app`.\n\nReadings on `origin/main` (`1c0152c91`):\n\n- `a_retract_above_the_part_hops_clean`: `[RapidInPart { at: 368 }, RapidInPart { at: 394 }]`. Move 367 is a Feed that ends at `(12.113734, -14.31511, 8.904555)`. Move 368 is a vertical Rapid from that point up to z 25.\n- `a_retract_below_the_high_run_never_takes_the_tool_into_the_part`: `[RapidInPart { at: 361 }, RapidInPart { at: 387 }]`, the same retracts.\n- `inside_first_on_a_convex_part_with_a_low_retract_never_digs_in`: `RapidInPart { at: 349 }`. Move 348 is a Feed that ends at `(4.0, -6.317902, 8.904555)` on the mesa side. Move 349 goes straight up from there to z 25.\n\nEach flagged move is an upward retract out of the end pose of a finish cut. The hops are correct. The finding is false.\n\n## Fix\n\n`judged()` in `crates/sim/src/verify/solid.rs` already has a rule for this case (`stack_hits`, the Area and Boundary reading). An upward vertical rapid that starts where a cut ended is judged like this:\n\n- the shank and the holder are swept over the full rapid;\n- the cutting edge is judged by the column that it rises into above its own top, at its largest radius;\n- the start pose stays with the law of the cut.\n\nThe envelope sweep now uses the same rule (`stack_only || ex.vertical_rapids_only`). The #4062 fault stays refused: a retract through a roof hits the rise column. `thin_disc_retract_hits_canopy` and `dovetail_retract_hits_canopy` start at the end of a Feed, and they still give `RapidInPart { at: 1 }`. Descents and rapids that do not start at a cut keep the full sweep.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/4211-envelope-lift-from-cut.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion --test finish3d_hop_height`: 5 passed (3 red before the fix).\n- `camcraft-sim --test vertical_rapid_part`: 7 passed. The new pin `a_retract_from_a_finish_touch_on_the_wall_stays_clear` fails without the fix (`RapidInPart { at: 1 }`) and passes with it. It is added to the existing #4062 suite.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick`) on head `374e538c6`, on Windows: 11 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The steps are the `camcraft-sim` lib, `mark_retract`, `midmove_pose`, `vertical_rapid_part`, `camcraft-motion` `solid_law`, and `camcraft-app` `probe_reach`, `real_tip_contour`, `thread_mill_rim`, `tool_body_drill_probe`.\n- Strict clippy on `camcraft-sim` and `camcraft-motion` (`--all-targets`): clean.\n- The `example_catalog*` suites did not run. No toolpath or post changes, so the catalog output does not change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The light lane: the change touches no heavy test.\n- No toolpath changes. The change only removes a false refusal of the verifier, so no posted G-code changes for a program that posted before.\n\nChangelog: Fix: a 3D finish pass that ends on a wall no longer has its retract refused as a rapid in the part (a false finding since #4062).\n\nEffort: low (fix in one function of `camcraft-sim`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4211\n",
